// Research paths (this game's own rules, not FFH2's; docs/PORTING.md, "Changes from FFH2").
//     A player commits to one path at a time. While committed, its research on the path's techs
//     runs RESEARCH_PATH_PERCENT percent faster (rules_defines.jsonc; a unique feature's bonus on
//     the same tech does not add to it: the larger counts). Once the player knows every tech of
//     the path it is complete, and the player may commit to another path. A completed path
//     cannot be taken again.
//
//     techs:           the techs the commitment speeds up; a tech may be on several paths
//     alignment_techs: the tech each alignment adds to the path, following the player's
//                      alignment of the moment
//     capstones:       the path's late techs. A civilization may commit to the path only if one
//                      of them (or the path's tech for its alignment) unlocks a unit it can train
//                      (no hero, no unit that needs a religion), unless none of them unlocks a
//                      unit for any civilization
//     bonus:           the resource the commitment grants at the capital, kept for good
[
  {
    "type": "RESEARCHPATH_ARCANE",
    "description": "TXT_KEY_RESEARCHPATH_ARCANE",
    "techs": ["TECH_KNOWLEDGE_OF_THE_ETHER", "TECH_ALTERATION", "TECH_DIVINATION", "TECH_ELEMENTALISM", "TECH_NECROMANCY", "TECH_SORCERY", "TECH_ARCANE_LORE", "TECH_STRENGTH_OF_WILL", "TECH_PASS_THROUGH_THE_ETHER"],
    "capstones": ["TECH_STRENGTH_OF_WILL", "TECH_PASS_THROUGH_THE_ETHER"],
    "bonus": "BONUS_REAGENTS"
  },
